    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d33">

                <pb facs="0039" n="29" xml:id="pg29"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/5–2649: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-26T17:00:00+01:00">May 26, 1949—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 26—1:29 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Actel 13. [For] Humelsine<anchor n="62" xml:id="d33-f1"/> from Battle.<anchor
                        n="63" xml:id="d33-f2"/> French Foreign Office indicated to Embassy last
                    week that Schuman<anchor n="64" xml:id="d33-f3"/> would like discuss with Sec at
                    some point question recognition Chinese Commies. In light Vishinsky proposal
                    Monday CFM and current developments China, let us have Dept. recommendation. In
                    case you recommend interview forward any material not in problem summary 61 or
                    available to Embassy advisers.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d33-f4"/> [Battle.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d33-f1" n="62" xml:id="d33-f1-content">
                <p>Carlisle H. Humelsine, Director of the Executive Secretariat of the Office of the
                    Secretary.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d33-f2" n="63" xml:id="d33-f2-content">
                <p>Lucius D. Battle, of the Executive Secretariat staff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d33-f3" n="64" xml:id="d33-f3-content">
                <p>Robert Schuman, French Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d33-f4" n="65" xml:id="d33-f4-content">
                <p>In reply, Mr. Humelsine reported in telegram Telac No. 26, May 28, the gist of
                    the replies to Department’s circular telegram of May 6, p.17.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
